// The same records under a `forbid`. The first `Read` shares the `Logout`'s nested id and not its
// "user.id": the forbid blocks it. The second has bob's nested id and alice's in its "user.id":
// allowed. A request environment that gave the two paths one key would allow the first and deny
// the second.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource);
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Logout"::response{ input.user.id: context.input.user.id }
};
